# ============================================================
# DeepSentinel — VAE-With-DSAA
# R26-IT-121 | IT22109194 | Wijesinghe L P D B
# ============================================================
# Rule of thumb: source, configuration and evidence are TRACKED.
# Data, trained weights and anything large are IGNORED and regenerable —
# see data/README.md and checkpoints/README.md for the exact commands.
#
# Order matters: git applies the LAST matching pattern, so the explicit
# re-inclusions at the bottom must stay at the bottom.

# ─── Large binary artefacts (regenerable) ──────────────────────────────
*.csv
*.npz
*.keras
*.h5
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.parquet
*.npy

# ─── Data and checkpoint trees ─────────────────────────────────────────
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
checkpoints/*
models/*
results/v4/data/
results/v4/curves/

# ─── Personal / other members' material ────────────────────────────────
MY CV/
Research Proposals/

# ─── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ─── Jupyter / IDE / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
wandb/

# ============================================================
# RE-INCLUSIONS — must remain last
# ============================================================
# Keep the directory placeholders and the READMEs that explain how to
# regenerate everything ignored above.
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
!checkpoints/README.md
!models/.gitkeep

# Source, tests and runnable wrappers are always tracked.
!src/**/*.py
!scripts/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.py

# Measured evidence and configuration are always tracked: the JSON metrics
# and the figures are what the results rest on, and they are small.
# Markdown is deliberately absent here — the write-ups are excluded at the
# bottom of this file, and a re-inclusion at this point would undo that.
!reports/**/*.json
!reports/**/*.png
!configs/*.yaml
!configs/*.yml
!docs/**
!examples/**
!notebooks/**

# ─── Overrides for the repo-root .gitignore ────────────────────────────
# The root file carries `VAE-With-DSAA/**/*.py` and a repo-wide `*.json`,
# written when this component was notebook-only. A deeper .gitignore wins,
# so these re-inclusions are what keep the dashboard and the demo fixture
# tracked. Without them `git add` succeeds silently and the files are simply
# absent from the repository.
!dashboard/**/*.py
!data/demo/*.json
!checkpoints/.gitkeep

# The v4 bundles are committed, unlike the raw weights `checkpoints/*` was
# written for: the whole tree is 870 KB of small .pt/.pkl/.json files, and
# without them nobody can start the service or reproduce the ablation from a
# clean clone. The directory has to be re-included before the files — git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, so a pattern matching only the files
# inside it would never be reached.
!checkpoints/v4/
!checkpoints/v4/**

# ─── Kept local, deliberately ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These have to sit after the re-inclusions above rather than with the
# other ignores: git applies the LAST matching pattern, and `!docs/**`
# would otherwise pull the proposal straight back in.
#
# The proposal is a personal submission rather than part of the component.
# The report markdown is a working record written for one reader — candid
# about limitations and easy to misread without its context — so it stays
# on disk and out of the repository. What those write-ups measure is still
# tracked: reports/**/*.json and reports/figures are untouched.
#
# Matched at any depth, not just `reports/*.md`: nothing else in either
# .gitignore excludes markdown, so a write-up in a subdirectory would
# otherwise be added by a plain `git add .` without anyone noticing.
docs/proposal/
reports/**/*.md
